<title>USA: Chaparral says Texas ups bid to $15.50/shr.</title>
<headline>Chaparral says Texas ups bid to $15.50/shr.</headline>
<dateline>MIDLOTHIAN, Texas 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chaparral Steel Co said Friday Texas Industries Inc upped its takeover bid for the company to $15.50 a share from $14.25 a share.</p>
<p>Chaparral said May 22 Texas Industries would pay its shareholders $14.25 a share in the unsolicited takeover offer. The recycled steelmaker said Texas Industries already owned 85 percent of its shares.</p>
<p>The company said it referred the revised offer to a special committee for consideration.</p>
<p>Chaparral's stock rose to 15-1/4 Friday early afternoon, up 5/16.</p>
